P18-V01 RequestResponseFuture and RequestFutureHolder implementation:
- Added public mutable `RequestResponseFuture` state, async latch, typed callback
  contract and exactly-once callback execution in Core. The process-wide
  `RequestFutureTable` now stores the same future entries used by Producer
  request registration, inbound reply completion, send failure and expiry.
- Re-exported the future/table/holder through Producer and the primary facade.
  Producer startup/shutdown manages a process-wide timeout scanner using the
  pinned three-second initial delay and one-second period; unregistering an
  individual Producer leaves pending futures in the live table.
- Runtime-owned scans are scoped to their registry while the public holder scan
  sees the process-wide table. This preserves runtime isolation with a shared
  table. The latch countdown uses an atomic watch update, and its concurrent
  regression passes.
- The first combined Core run exposed cross-test correlation-key collisions,
  global expiry crossing runtime boundaries, and an exact-deadline test relying
  on a request future created after its deadline timestamp. Scoped expiry,
  test-specific keys and a post-deadline clock assertion fixed these issues.
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-core --all-features --locked` — PASS (163
  Core unit tests; all Core integration and doc-test targets pass).
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-producer -p rocketmq-classic --all-features
  --locked` — PASS (142 Producer unit tests; request/reply timeout, send-failure,
  shutdown and facade live-table tests; all selected integration/doc targets).
- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D
  warnings` — PASS.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` — PASS.
- Updated the Phase 15 request/reply matrix and release checklist. This closes
  the public future/live-table request/reply slice only. Broad P18-V01, the
  full current-tree P18-V02 rerun, current GitHub Ubuntu/P18-V04 evidence,
  Phase 19 Docker/Broker automation, and pre-publication version/registry
  resolution remain open. Owner-run deployment and production checks remain
  Phase 19 manual validation.
- No Java checkout changes, Docker/live Broker run, plan edits, push, tag,
  publication or deployment.
